{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/674972-knowledge-and-the-tempest","id":674972,"title":"Knowledge and the Tempest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T00:08:08-07:00","id":674972,"title":"Knowledge and the Tempest","content":"We all know that the Tempest carries in it the knowledge of those who have died, but how far does that go? Would you say it's possible to discover the lost Gifts of extinct Fera in the Tempest? Perhaps the knowledge of Changeling Arts and the secrets of those who died by Cold Iron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T01:08:40-07:00","id":675016,"title":"","content":"Anything is possible if you are running the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T05:11:09-07:00","id":675131,"title":"","content":"Under standard WoD cosmology I would say you have an Unstoppable Force Immovable Object conundrum. Fera gifts are very much a spirit thing, aka Middle Umbra. Dead Fera really have no interaction with the Low Umbra, let alone the Tempest. Same for Fae, they are creatures of the Dreaming, which is either its own Umbra or a part of the Middle Umbra. How would that knowledge even get there to be found?<br /> <br /> And yet... The Low Umbra is memory; that's its entire theme. That and the remnants of all things circling the drain of Oblivion. Even the Wyrm will (allegedly) end up falling to Oblivion. So it is very much in keeping that things past, even those that shouldn't be there, would be there.<br /> <br /> I'd ask this question: Are they actually gone and annihilated? If the answer is no, and their souls and ancestral spirits still lurk in some dark corner of the Umbra (or Dreaming), then you can't find their knowledge in the Tempest. Their physical forms may be gone but what they <i>are</i> is still very much alive. If, on the other hand, they've been stripped from the world, then their last remnants are still swirling around in the tank of the Tempest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:06:59-07:00","id":713068,"title":"","content":"I've always played the Dreaming as a Zone that can touch upon the Low Umbra tbh, a sort of crossroads where a Sandman and mortal could meet in the realm of sleep. Of course that's just the regular mortal dreamscape part of the Dreaming and not a place easily reached for a mortal or wraith that wants in there. I do know that essentially low-level Sandmen fiddle with dreamers by plucking them into the Shadowlands and Phantasm 2 can mold how the mortal dreamer sees the Shadowlands/Tempest etcetra around them, but hey... What can I say, I'm a sucker for exploring the Umbra and crossovers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I still ponder on links between the Labyrinth and the Black Spiral Labyrinth, though one leads to Oblivion, the second to Morfeas. Two seperate places, though perhaps one could cross from one Labyrinth to the other. ^^<br /> <br /> On-topic, I don't know much about W:tA, though I always figured dead Garou went somewhere other than the Shadowlands/Tempest at their demise. And yet still, some kind of info they may have imparted to mortal hands could be there, perhaps, or a book/tome that a mortal happened to read. Also the Tempest is as much a physical place (in a sense) as a person's mind made form. I'd leave it to Storyteller caveat, seeing as how maleable the Tempest can be, depending on the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T05:48:43-07:00","id":714249,"title":"","content":"The Labyrinth and the Black Spiral Labyrinth are implicitly connected. In The Book of Madness, the sleeping Malfeans' dreams have become semi-autonomous beings, some of which might exist in Malfeas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T09:22:42-07:00","id":729107,"title":"","content":"I was going to say that's too tenuous a connection to matter, but with the Maelstroms the Labyrinth belches out that would be an excellent mechanism for dread knowledge and terrible blasphemies to get into the Tempest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}